{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__English__Grammar__Error_Detection__jivk1_hn_mocks_wallah","path":"organized/Others/English/Grammar/Error Detection/jivk1_hn_mocks_wallah.html","title":"Mocks Wallah - Noun Quiz","provider":"organized","category":"Others/English/Grammar/Error Detection","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":25,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">He has been looking</span></span></span></p>","<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">for an interesting work</span></span></span></p>","<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">for a long time</span></span></span></p>","<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Cambria, serif; font-size: 19px;\">No error</span></p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Work is an uncountable noun</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">. Hence use of definite article AN is wrong with it. The correct usage will be - </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>An interesting Piece of work.</strong></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Concept - </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"A\" and \"an\" are indefinite articles used to modify singular countable nouns. Uncountable nouns, also known as mass nouns, do not have a plural form and cannot be counted, so they do not use \"a\" or \"an\". </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Taj Mahal is made of white marble</p>","<p>while most of the buildings</p>","<p>built during the Mughal</p>","<p>empire are made of redstones</p>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is in the word \"stones\". Here, \"stone\" is being used as an uncountable noun, referring to a building material. In this context, it should not be pluralized. </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Red Stone</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> will be the correct usage. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Such social programmes</p>","<p>provide all social stratums</p>","<p>with an opportunity to share</p>","<p>a common social platform</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stratum</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is a singular noun, and \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>strata</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is its plural form. </span></span></span> <br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">In this context, \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>strata</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is the correct word to use, as it refers to multiple layers or levels of society. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>The company's management team consists</p>","<p>of a group of experienced professionals</p>","<p>with extensive knowledges in their fields</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"Knowledges\" should be replaced with \"knowledge\", as \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>knowledge</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is an uncountable noun. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>The teacher gave the student</p>","<p>a huge list of book to</p>","<p>read during the summer vacation</p>","<p>no error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is in the word \"book\". Here, \"book\" is a countable noun, and it should be in the plural form \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>books</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" because the phrase \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>a huge list</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" implies that there are many books. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>The issues are very complex</p>","<p>and the problem is that they</p>","<p>are bound to be obscured</p>","<p>by these hypocritical politician.</p>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The correct word should be \"politicians\", which is a plural noun. </span></span></span> <br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>These + Plural Noun</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> is the correct usage. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>You will not be</p>","<p>allowed to go anywhere</p>","<p>else to play outdoor games</p>","<p>no error</p>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The sentence is grammatically correct. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>An earthquake is a</p>","<p>natural phenomena and nobody</p>","<p>can check it, be sure.</p>","<p>No Error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>phenomena</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is a plural noun, and it should be replaced with the singular noun \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>phenomenon</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\".</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Corrected sentence: An earthquake is a natural </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>phenomenon</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> and nobody can check it, be sure. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>The company has decided</p>","<p>to recruit a large number of employees</p>","<p>to work in its new branch.</p>","<p>no error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that \"employee\" should be replaced with \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>employees</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\", as \"employees\" is a plural noun and agrees with the phrase \"a large number of\".</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>A large number of + Plural Noun</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> is the correct usage. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>The Billy goat</p>","<p>gave birth</p>","<p>to a kid</p>","<p>No Error</p>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Billy</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> goats are </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>MALE</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> & being male, they cannot give birth. </span></span></span> <br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Female</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> goats, also known as </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>does</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> or </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>nannies</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">, give birth.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Corrected sentence: The </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>nanny</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> goat gave birth to a kid. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Summons after summons</p>","<p>were issued</p>","<p>by the court</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that the subject \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>SUMMONS</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is a </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>singular</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> noun, and it should be paired with the singular verb \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>was issued</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" instead of the plural verb \"were issued\".</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Plural form is Summons is - </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>SUMMONSES</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">. </span></span></span> </p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>In my opinion</p>","<p>police is still</p>","<p>investigating that case</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>police</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is a </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>plural</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> noun, and it should be paired with the plural verb \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>are</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" instead of the singular verb \"is\". </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>The committee comprise</p>","<p>five members who</p>","<p>are experts in their field</p>","<p>no error</p>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that the verb \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>comprise</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" should be replaced with \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>comprises</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\", as \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>committee</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is a singular noun.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Important Note</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">: \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Comprise</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" means to consist of or be made up of, and it's often used incorrectly with </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>OF</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">. The correct usage is:</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The committee comprises of five members. Incorrect</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The committee comprises five members. Correct </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>As he didn't have</p>","<p>any pen, I told him</p>","<p>the address verbally</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Verbally</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" and \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Orally</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" are often used interchangeably, but there is a subtle difference:</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Orally</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" typically refers to communication that occurs through spoken words, often in a formal or official context. For example:</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The doctor gave the patient oral instructions.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The teacher gave an oral exam.</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Verbally</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\", on the other hand, can refer to communication that occurs through spoken or written words. It often implies a more explicit or direct form of communication. For example:</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The manager verbally abused the employee.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The company verbally agreed to the terms.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>In the context of the original sentence: </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Both \"verbally\" and \"orally\" could work, but \"orally\" might be a slightly better choice to convey the idea that the address was communicated through spoken words. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Mrs Verma became</p>","<p>envious when she saw her</p>","<p>husband with Mrs Shukla</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>envious</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" should be replaced with \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>jealous</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\", as \"envious\" typically implies a desire for something someone else has, whereas \"jealous\" implies a sense of insecurity or threat.</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Envious</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" typically implies a desire for something someone else has, often with a sense of resentment or bitterness. For example:</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- She was envious of her friend's success.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- He was envious of his neighbour’s luxurious car.</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Jealous</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\", on the other hand, typically implies a sense of insecurity or threat, often related to a personal relationship or possession. For example:</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- She was jealous of the attention her partner was giving to someone else.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- He was jealous of his brother's influence over their parents.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>To illustrate the difference:</strong></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- If someone has a nice car, you might be envious of their car.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- But if your partner is spending too much time with someone else, you might be jealous of the attention they're receiving.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>In the context of the original sentence: </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Both words could work, but \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>jealous</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" might be a slightly better choice to convey the idea that Mrs Verma feels threatened or insecure about her relationship with her husband. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>I tried taking tablets for</p>","<p>the headache, but they did not</p>","<p>not have any affect.</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Replace </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>AFFECT</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> with </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>EFFECT</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">. </span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Affect</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> is a </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>verb</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> that means to have an influence on someone or something or to cause a change in someone or something. </span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">For example - Both buildings were badly affected by the fire.</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Effect</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> is a noun that means the result of a particular influence. </span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">For example - I think I’m suffering from the effects of too little sleep.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Correct sentence: ‘I tried taking tablets for the headache, but they did not have any effect.’</strong></span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>For your and your</p>","<p>wife sake, find a job</p>","<p>and stop wasting time</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The original phrase \"for your wife sake\" is grammatically incorrect. The corrected phrase \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>for your wife's sake</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is a common idiomatic expression that means \"for the benefit or well-being of your wife\". </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>John and Merry's</p>","<p>homes are on the opposite</p>","<p>sides of the road</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The error is that the possessive form \"John and Merry's\" implies that John and Merry </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>jointly</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> own the homes.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Corrected sentence</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">: </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>John's and Merry's</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> homes are on the opposite sides of the road.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">By changing the possessive form to \"John's and Merry's\", we indicate that John and Merry each own a separate home. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Kapil dev said that Sachin's</p>","<p>and Sehwag's partnership</p>","<p>was very impressive</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Use of apostrophe with Sachin is incorrect here. </span></span></span> <br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Sachin and Sehwag's</strong></span></span></span> <span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>partnership</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> will be the correct usage as the century is made in partnership. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>An ellipse has</p>","<p>two focus and a circle</p>","<p>has only one centre</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Replace </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>FOCUS</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> with </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>FOCI </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">as the plural form of Focus is </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>FOCI</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Lalu Yadav has nine</p>","<p>offsprings still he faces</p>","<p>no problem in providing them food</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Offsprings</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is not a commonly used word in English, and \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>offspring</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" is the preferred term to refer to the children of a person or animal. So, Replace </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Offsprings</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> with </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Offspring</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> to make the sentence grammatically correct. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Attorney-generals from 16 states</p>","<p>condemned the ban yesterday and</p>","<p>were discussing whether to challenge it</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Compound words make their plural by changing their keyword into plural form. Here, key word is ‘attorney’. Therefore, it should be ‘</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Attorneys-general’</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> in place of </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Attorney-generals</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> to make the sentence grammatically correct.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Correct sentence:</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong> Attorneys-general from 16 states condemned the ban yesterday and were discussing whether to challenge it.</strong></span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\"/></span></span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\">The\nfollowing sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the\nsegment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span><br/>","options":["Please tell him","that my father has","sent him regard","No error"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\">Replace\n</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\"><b>REGARD</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\">\nwith </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\"><b>REGARDS</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\">.</span></span></span><br/><span style=\"color: #000000\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px\">The\nword \"regards\" is a plural noun, and it's commonly used in\nexpressions of goodwill or greetings, such as \"send regards\"\nor \"best regards\". </span></span></span>\n<br/>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Radha bought a sheet of paper</p>","<p>from the stationary and</p>","<p>wrote something on it</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Replace </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stationary</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> with </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stationery</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stationary</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" and \"</span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stationery</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">\" are two words that are often confused with each other due to their similar spellings, but they have very different meanings:</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stationary</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> adjective:- Means not moving or remaining in one place. Examples:</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The car is stationary.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> <span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The bike is stationary on the rack.</span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>Stationery</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> noun: Refers to writing and office supplies, such as paper, pens, pencils, and envelopes. Examples:</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- I need to buy some stationery for my office.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> <span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">- The store sells a variety of stationery items.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>To help you remember the difference:</strong></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">If you can replace the word with \"not moving\", use \"stationary\".</span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"justify\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1056px; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 15px;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">If you're talking about office supplies, use \"stationery\". </span></span></span></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"},{"question":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.</span></span></p>","options":["<p>Many summons</p>","<p>have been issued</p>","<p>to Rahul Gandhi so far</p>","<p>No error</p>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">Use </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>SUMMONSES</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> in place of </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>SUMMONS </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">as we need a plural noun with </span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>MANY</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\">.</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>SUMMONS</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> is a singular noun. </span></span></span> <br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"><strong>SUMMONSES</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria,serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 19px;\"> is a plural noun. </span></span></span></p>","marks":2,"section":"Noun"}]}